          "schema": "QurlMintTargetPath",
          "keyword": "description",
          "expected": "Destination path and optional query for a qURL Connector link. For example,\n`/view/abc?download=1` redirects to that path on the resource's `qurl.site` host.\nOmit this field to use the host's root. Only qURL Connector resources (`type=tunnel`)\naccept it. Maximum: 2048 UTF-8 bytes.\n\n**Access scope:** The path permits itself and descendants at a segment boundary.\n`/view/abc` permits `/view/abc/thumbnail`, but not `/view/abcd`.\nThe query does not restrict access. A scoped link works only through the resource\nhost; access through a custom domain is denied. The Connector must also authorize\nthe path before using it to look up an object.\n\n**Path rules:** Start with one `/`. Use canonical, unescaped ASCII. A single trailing\nslash is allowed. Do not use `//`, percent escapes, semicolons, empty interior\nsegments, `.` or `..` segments, exclamation marks, parentheses, asterisks, apostrophes,\na scheme, host, backslash, fragment, whitespace, or control characters.\nUse opaque route keys for objects; keep user filenames in metadata.\nClients must preserve the accepted path bytes. Percent-encoded alternatives are denied.\n\n**Query rules:** Use ASCII letters, digits, `._~!$&()*+,;=:@/?-`, and well-formed\npercent escapes. Percent-encode other characters. Literal apostrophes are not\naccepted. Query bytes are preserved, including semicolons and percent escapes.\n\n**Errors:** JSON null and non-string values return `400 validation_error`.\nEmpty strings, oversized or malformed paths, and use on other resource types\nreturn `400 invalid_target_path`.\n"
        }
